    "domain_separator_must_appear": "trtx402:v1:"
  },
  "notes": [
    "ADR-054-001: component (d) of binding hash is sha256(jcs(settlement_evidence_subset)) with 6 canonical fields. Block-level fields (blockHeight, confirmations, observedAt) are NOT part of the subset — only the 6 fields enumerated in must_hash_settlement_subset_fields are hashed.",
    "Adversarial scenario: txHash tampering. An agent attempts to bind its receipt to a different on-chain settlement (e.g. claiming a third party's tx as proof of its own payment). The binding hash rejects because txHash is part of the canonical settlement subset.",
    "This vector tests the most economically critical mismatch: a verifier that fails to detect a settlement tx swap would accept fraudulent proofs of payment. The typed reason 'binding_mismatch' with mismatched_component 'settlement_evidence_subset' is the audit-grade signal.",
    "Test runner MUST recompute binding hash using verification_inputs.settlement_evidence (6-field subset per binding-components-manifest v1.0.0) and assert hash != binding_hash_declared."
  ],
